{
  "key": "gh-690",
  "fields": {
    "summary": "pack-release: empty bump PRs merge when content lands mid-flight (no nothing-changed guard) + sm_github version skew 0.1.24 vs 0.1.23",
    "description": "Live 2026-10-04 05:40-05:48: three content PRs (#684/#685/#686) merged within 3 min → release automation produced THREE bump PRs (#687/#688/#689) and **#689 merged with a 0-byte diff** (its branch was cut before #688 landed; merge message literally shows 'Merge branch main into chore/pack-versions/20261004-054742'). An empty PR rode the full review/merge cycle.

Fix: when the bump branch finds main already carries the target versions (empty diff), CLOSE the PR instead of merging (or skip creating it). Also check the double-trigger: one content merge batch produced overlapping bump runs (concurrency group missing?).

Secondary: latest release agents-rel-20261004-054747 ships sm_github-0.1.24.zip while every other agent is 0.1.23 — one extra bump for sm_github; audit the version ledger for the off-by-one.

